that took the most mass, which is what \code{item_report()} counts as \code{n_won}.

\code{"uncertain"} is a rank rather than a threshold in both cases, so it commits
to no cut point. On two labels it sorts by distance from 0.5. Above two it
sorts by \code{margin}, the gap between the winning label and the runner-up, so
the first rows are the closest calls.
